sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    participant Page as Admin sites page<br/>/admin/sites<br/>EditSiteModal
    participant SitePage as Site page<br/>/detail/[namesite]<br/>SitePageEditor
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Admin,DB: Covers US 2.0.3 and 2.0.5. Both parts exist in the code. updateSite, toggleSiteActive and updateSitePageFields<br/>check the caller on the server with requireApprovedAdmin(). getSitePageFields reads with the signed-in session.<br/><br/>Part 1: US 2.0.3 Deactivate or reactivate a Site
    Admin->>Page: Open EditSiteModal, set Active on or off, select Save (AT1)
    activate Page
    Page->>Actions: handleSaveSite: updateSite(id, namesite, ab_county, protectedAreaId), then<br/>toggleSiteActive(id, is_active) only if is_active changed
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
    alt Caller is not an Admin
        Actions-->>Page: Throw 'Only admins can edit sites.', no change
        Page-->>Admin: alert() with the error
    else Caller is an Admin
        Actions->>DB: Update sites_pa namesite, ab_county, protected_area_id,<br/>then is_active only if it changed
        activate DB
        alt Update fails
            DB-->>Actions: Error (a duplicate name or a protected area that is already linked gives a clear message)
            Actions-->>Page: Throw error
            Page-->>Admin: alert() with the error
        else Update done
            DB-->>Actions: OK
            Actions-->>Page: OK
            Page-->>Admin: Show the new status in the list
        end
        deactivate DB
    end
    deactivate Actions
    deactivate Page
    Note over Admin,DB: createSite inserts is_active = true, so a new Site is active (AT5). getSitesOnline reads only active Sites, so an inactive Site<br/>leaves the Site list, pickers and search (AT2) and the map boundaries (is_active !== false), and returns after reactivation (AT3).<br/>Gap for AT4: getSiteByName returns an inactive Site, but the Site page throws "This site is not active",<br/>so its SIRs cannot be opened there. This is not fixed.<br/><br/>Part 2: US 2.0.5 Update the fields of a Site page
    Admin->>SitePage: Open the Site page
    activate SitePage
    SitePage->>Actions: getSiteLinks(siteId) and getSitePageFields(siteId)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>DB: Select field_key, value, is_visible from site_page_fields for the Site<br/>(the signed-in session, RLS allows signed-in users)
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Rows
    deactivate DB
    Actions-->>SitePage: Fields. getSiteLinks returns only the visible links.
    deactivate Actions
    alt Caller is not an Admin (AT2)
        SitePage-->>Admin: No "Edit site page" button. The Site page stays in view mode.
    else Caller is an Admin (AT1)
        Admin->>SitePage: Select "Edit site page"
        SitePage-->>Admin: Show each field from SITE_PAGE_FIELDS (SAPAA website, iNaturalist, designated steward)<br/>with a Shown or Hidden toggle (AT3)
        Admin->>SitePage: Change the links, toggle Shown or Hidden, select Save
        SitePage->>Actions: updateSitePageFields(siteId, fields)
        activate Actions
        Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedAdmin()
        alt Caller is not an Admin
            Actions-->>SitePage: Throw 'Only admins can edit sites.'
            SitePage-->>Admin: Show the error and stay in the editor
        else Caller is an Admin
            Actions->>Actions: Reject an unknown field_key. Reject a link that does not start with http:// or https://.
            Actions->>DB: Upsert site_page_fields on (site_id, field_key) with value, is_visible,<br/>updated_by and updated_at
            activate DB
            alt Validation or update fails
                DB-->>Actions: Error
                Actions-->>SitePage: Throw error
                SitePage-->>Admin: Show the error and stay in the editor
            else Update done
                DB-->>Actions: OK
                Actions-->>SitePage: OK
                SitePage->>Actions: getSiteLinks(siteId) and getSitePageFields(siteId) again
                SitePage-->>Admin: Show the visible links and drop the hidden fields (AT4)
            end
            deactivate DB
        end
        deactivate Actions
    end
    deactivate SitePage

    Note over Admin,DB: A hidden field keeps its saved value. The designated steward field only shows or hides the steward.<br/>The steward is assigned with the Steward control on the Site page (US 3.0.2), not in this editor.<br/>An Admin still sees a hidden steward so the assignment can be managed.
